Fused panel fill (Loom AIE2P array programs): GEMM workers fill their own memory-tile panels, so weights can be decoded
by the cores that use them (no decoder column).
- Data core streams may be multicast: a binding sender feeding several workers' core streams (constrain.core_stream
  on each channel of one sender) takes one shim MM2S; followers route from the owner's shim channel. Streamed plans
  give such supplies a descriptor set per parity, and the control program pushes them as call bindings.
- Panels filled from worker egress (constrain.fill): each source fills its own panel; channels with the same fill
  source share it (a filling row's panel also holds the next row's slice).
